{
  "id": "COMPOUND:19233 - PROTEIN:5817",
  "verbalization": "Trichothecolone is implicated in the targeting of HepG2 cells through multiple pathways, with SNU-387 serving as a common intermediate in these relationships. The drug is directly linked to SNU-387, which in turn targets HepG2, suggesting a potential mechanism of action involving the modulation of cellular processes in these cancerous cells. The presence of multiple targets, including Dendocarbin K and Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside, further supports a broad interaction with HepG2, potentially through distinct molecular mechanisms. The final scores from the paths indicate a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The integration of these findings suggests that Trichothecolone may exert its effects on HepG2 via a complex network of targets, possibly involving cellular signaling pathways that are dysregulated in this cell line.",
